Now, is there a risk that "空白折成连字符" means each whitespace char becomes a hyphen (so "a  b" -> "a--b")? The phrase "折成连字符" typically means convert whitespace to hyphens; collapsing runs is the standard URL-slug behavior, and "首尾不留" suggests trimming. I'll go with collapse and document the decision in my report. This is the reasonable default. Since the user said "怎么落地你定", collapsing is my call.

